        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A premium visual breakdown of how a subtle rumble under load became a snapped crankshaft, destroyed bottom end, and a £7,610 reconditioned engine replacement."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I heard a rumble under load when towing the caravan. It was subtle — I thought it might be a wheel bearing or exhaust heat shield. I ignored it for a few weeks. Then one morning on the M6, there was a loud bang from the engine bay, the oil pressure light flashed, and the accelerator pedal went dead. By the time I coasted to the hard shoulder, the engine had locked solid. The AA man said, ‘That’s not a bearing — that’s a snapped crank.’”"
        },
