      {
        "id": "the-whole-disaster-started-with-a-subtle-rumble-under-load",
        "title": "The whole disaster started with a subtle rumble under load.",
        "description": "The sound was most noticeable when towing uphill. The owner dismissed it as a wheel bearing or exhaust heat shield. Within 4,000 miles, the crankshaft snapped, destroying the engine.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/1.2-land-rover-discovery3-tdv6-snapped-crank.png",
            "alt": "Land Rover TDV6 crankshaft snapped in two pieces after catastrophic failure",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What owner thought"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“Probably a wheel bearing”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The vehicle still drove normally, so the symptom did not feel urgent."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What it actually was"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Bottom-end bearing wear"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The TDV6 crank bearings were wearing, allowing the crank to flex and eventually snap."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Why it matters"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Catastrophic snap"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Once the crank snaps, the block is destroyed. Land Rover does not authorise third-party rebuilds."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "If your Discovery 3 TDV6 develops a rumble under load — especially when towing — have the bottom end inspected immediately. Ignoring it can lead to a snapped crankshaft and a £7,000+ engine replacement."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Failure timeline"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "the-whole-disaster-started-with-a-subtle-rumble-under-load",
          "order": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "from-a-subtle-rumble-to-a-snapped-crank-in-just-4-000-miles",
        "title": "From a subtle rumble to a snapped crank in just 4,000 miles.",
        "description": "This case is a classic catastrophic TDV6 crankshaft failure: the owner ignored the warning signs and paid the price.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/2.2-land-rover-discovery3-tdv6-timeline.png",
            "alt": "Land Rover Discovery 3 TDV6 timeline from rumble to snapped crankshaft",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What the owner noticed"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A subtle rumble under load became a snapped crankshaft at 65mph within 4,000 miles."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What was happening internally"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Bottom-end bearings wore, the crank flexed and snapped, destroying the block and oil system."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“I nearly scrapped it. The repair cost more than the car was worth on paper. But what was I going to buy for £7,600- Another Discovery 3 with unknown history and the same risk- A reconditioned engine at least came with a warranty. I bit the bullet and paid £7,600 to keep it on the road. Two years later, it’s still going strong.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "138,000 miles"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Subtle rumble under load"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "142,000 miles"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Snapped crank at 65mph"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Specialist"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Reconditioned engine fitted"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Workshop diagnosis"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
