      {
        "id": "the-replacement-engine-was-not-the-only-question-debris-had-circulated-through-the-oil-system",
        "title": "The replacement engine was not the only question. Debris had circulated through the oil system.",
        "description": "With metal particles throughout the oil system, the specialist could not fully know whether the turbocharger had already been affected by debris contamination.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h3",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Path A"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Fit reconditioned long engine only. Keep existing turbocharger."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "£7,600"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "If turbo fails later: add £800–£1,200 + labour."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h3",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Path B"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Fit reconditioned long engine + new turbocharger."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "£8,800"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Higher upfront cost, but eliminates turbo failure risk."
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/5.1-land-rover-discovery3-tdv6-turbo-risk.png",
